### 20839290 2011 Effects of denosumab on bone turnover markers in postmenopausal osteoporosis.
pmid 20839290 nct NCT00089791 doi 10.1002/jbmr.251 pubtypes ['Journal Article', 'Randomized Controlled Trial']
- This study evaluates the time course and determinants of bone turnover marker (BTM) response during denosumab treatment, the percentage of denosumab-treated women with BTMs below the premenopausal reference interval, and the correlations between changes in BTMs and bone mineral density (BMD).
- The BTM substudy of the Fracture REduction Evaulation of Denosumab in Osteoporosis every 6 Months (FREEDOM) Trial included 160 women randomized to subcutaneous denosumab (60 mg) or placebo injections every 6 months for 3 years.
- With denosumab, but not placebo, there were significant correlations between CTX reduction and BMD increase (r = -0.24 to -0.44).

